{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And they said to him.</b> Pointed with a vowel on the vav of אֵלָיו. And it is taught in a Tannaitic source: Rabbi Shimon ben Elazar says — wherever Scripture points with a vowel, you expound the consonantal text; but here the pointing overrides the consonantal text — you expound the vowel marking. For they asked even about Sarah, where is Abraham — this teaches that a person should ask his host about the man concerning the woman, and about the woman concerning the man. In Bava Metzia they say: the ministering angels knew where Sarah our matriarch was, but only to make known that she was modest, so as to endear her to her husband. Rabbi Yossi ben Chanina said: in order to send her the cup of blessing." "<b>Here, in the tent.</b> She is modest."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Rashi's source for the reading 'wherever Scripture points… you expound the consonantal text' is apparently the Talmud Yerushalmi; 'the pointing overrides' reflects the tradition that the extra vowel mark on אֵלָיו signals the angels' additional address to Sarah."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:17.027407309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}